Z||000005||Doni Hagan||12-21-2001||11:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B>Hope you guys realize that the light covers on a Ferrari 308 are smooth and the louvers are BEHIND the lights.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, I realize that. I had one in the late 80's (during my Magnum P.I./Miami Vice stage.) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I wanted them on this car more to make it different than to ape the 308. Besides, they compliment the hood louvers. Once the car is finally painted, they'll make more sense aesthetically. I just painted them black for the purposes of the pictures. <P>Still, my hat's off to Pat......They're very well done! <P>||||reg||1
